      "message": "Here is a quick summary of why it is a highly correct and necessary security fix:\n\n  1. Crop Parameter Bounds Checks: It adds crucial validation to ensure crop parameters ( crop_x ,  crop_y ,  crop_width ,         \n  crop_height ) are non-negative and fit entirely within the source image dimensions, preventing out-of-bounds reads from the      \n  sample  buffer.\n  2. Overflow-Safe Temp Buffer Allocation: It changes buffer sizes to  size_t  and adds explicit overflow checks ( uv_size \u003e       \n  SIZE_MAX / 2  and  y_size \u003e SIZE_MAX - uv_size * 2 ) before allocating the rotation buffer, preventing heap overflows.\n  3. 64-bit Pointer Arithmetic Promotion: It casts  src_width  to  ptrdiff_t  in pointer offset calculations (e.g.,  sample +      \n  (ptrdiff_t)src_width * crop_y ). This forces the multiplication to be performed in 64-bit instead of 32-bit signed  int ,\n  preventing wrapping before adding to the pointer.",
